            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MISSJENAFFLECK"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This used to be my favorite menu item at my local bagel place when I was in college. If you add some thinly sliced red onions and lemon pepper, it is absolutley amazing! The lemon pepper is essential. Sounds weird but seriously you have to try it!!!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Misty"
            },
            "reviewBody": "EXCELLANT taste with the fresh basil! We substituted the cream cheese for a slice of swiss and it was delicious. I will recommend one suggestion that makes these tastier and easier to eat. After toasting and adding the cheese (either kind), lay the basil UNDER the tomatoes, and then broil the halves on a cookie sheet for 5-10 minutes. This will soften and roast the tomatoes just enough to make the sandwich easier to bite into. Placing the basil under the tomatoes keeps it from crisping into nothingness :)",
            "datePublished": "2008-08-08T19:34:16.593Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Stephanie Towery-Haines"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love these and eat them very often. Sometimes i used garlic ranch cream cheese (if i have it available) other wise plain is fine too. I often will add onion and or sliced cucumber. Or even rub some Italian dressing on the tomatoes. I always add basil (fresh if i have it). A slice of mozzarella slightly melted over top is a nice added touch too!",
            "datePublished": "2020-09-26T22:13:02.107Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sylvia Vickers"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved it because you can also make it with Vegan Cream cheese ! A sprinkle of Lemon Pepper or everything but the bagel seasoning also takes it up a notch!",
            "datePublished": "2021-09-03T07:20:01.767Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tanaquil"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Update: Tried this with fresh basil and cherry tomatoes from our garden, it was good. Used homemade bagels from this site (Bread machine bagels). Original review: This is one of my favorite quick lunches from this site. I have not tried with fresh basil, I always use dried. I have even added basil, tomato, &amp; cr. cheese into my Magic Bullet to make sandwich spread.",
            "datePublished": "2008-06-05T16:38:09.297Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JanieBeth"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious! Here's another variation that is wonderful: dark pumpernickel bread, thinly sliced tomato, thinly sliced red onion, cream cheese, smoked salmon. Omit the basil for this version.",
            "datePublished": "2015-06-10T06:10:23.577Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Molly"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Fantastic! I finally have fresh basil ready for the picking and I had some bagel thins, so this was lunch today. By using a 90 calorie bagel thin and fat-free cream cheese, this really dropped the calories in this sandwich. A delicious summer delight that I know will be lunch, many times this summer!",
            "datePublished": "2014-06-09T12:34:42.607Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Nikki McMahoon"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I just made this and loved it! Well I should say I made a version of this... didn't have bagles so I just used toasted bread, and I used spinach leaves instead of basil. Fantastic and so easy!",
            "datePublished": "2019-02-15T01:22:28.167Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TwoSweetPickles"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is more like a method than a recipe, but the original is very good. Looking forward to adding dill instead of basil, maybe some cucumber, smoked salmon or even an egg...the possibilities are many! Also, bagel thins instead of a bagel make this more carb-friendly for those of us who need that.",
            "datePublished": "2011-07-16T17:55:20.863Z"
          },
          {
